editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-53.md:95:It was harder than it had looked. A man had done it in three breaths with staves coming over a baulk at his head, and Cael, with nobody near him and all the dusk to do it in, found that he did not know where his own hip was. He brought the knee in over the heel. He let the shoulder down, and turned it. He was a long way off the line, and he could feel that he was, as a person feels a picture hanging crooked; and the thing that lay along him felt it too, and waited.
