+# Editorial review — Movement 008
+
+## Review status and coverage
+
+This is an informed AI editorial-seat review in a fresh working context, not a real-human read and not a blinded cold read: the supplied prompt included the full movement, canon evidence, protected wording, formula, and measured results. I read all seven supplied chapters in order (chapters 47–53). The narrative movement is present from start to finish, but the release text is not complete because ten coordinator placeholders remain in the manuscript.
+
+## Unscored reader response
+
+Interest caught when Teague began teaching Cael to read the ground in chapter 47, sharpened at the shale-back seep in chapter 48, and peaked in the Span fight and the blanket inquiry. It slipped during some of the route-and-record setup in chapters 47–48, then stopped outright whenever a long `[[TIER-B: ... coordinator to supply protected text]]` note replaced dialogue or narration. The young one matters most beyond Cael: his offered water, frightened crossing, ravine descent, and unasked-for care of the fallen broad man turn him from an anonymous burden into the person whose coming loss will hurt.
+
+I expect the notch/pass ahead to force the first consequential choice about Cael's new Force-adjacent capability and to test whether the wall contract can survive an ambush. I would continue. The field problem, the old line, and the evidence of an internal Compact dispute all open forward pressure; the placeholders must be repaired before this can function as a finished reader experience.
+
+## Reader scores
+
+The two columns are editorial lenses, not demographic research or a sales forecast. Scores are not averaged into a gate.
+
+| Dimension | Fluent thirteen-year-old | Adult genre reader | Exact passage location and reason | Confidence |
+|---|---:|---:|---|---|
+| Opening pull | 7 | 8 | Chapter 47, line 3, “for six hours nobody said a word,” followed by the unexplained sound behind them: concrete unease arrives immediately, though cord, file order, and route knowledge begin accumulating before the immediate danger resolves. | High |
+| Keep reading | 6 | 7 | Chapter 49, lines 169–171, the intended “Nobody declares…” rule and Teague's “Noted,” through chapter 50's width solution and chapter 53's notch reveal. The local payoff is strong, but ten visible editorial notes—including the final exchange at 53:291—repeatedly break immersion and withhold intended text. | High |
+| Interest / freshness | 8 | 9 | Chapter 48's shale-back seep; chapter 50, lines 151–209, where Teague notices width and five people cross stake thirty-four; chapter 52's evidence blanket. Problems are solved by terrain, rules, record craft, and restraint rather than generic force. | High |
+| Clarity / flow | 4 | 5 | Chapter 50, lines 113, 173, 177, and 245, where production notes interrupt the fight; chapter 52, lines 117–221, where the hide, clean sheet, six copied sheets, notebook table, folded paper, and three conceptual “pages” must all be retained at once. The underlying action is lucid, but the current file cannot be read cleanly in one pass. | High |
+| Character attachment | 8 | 9 | Chapter 51, line 123: the young one has run the shelf, protected the broad man's head, carried water, webbing, pannier, and blanket, then simply waits until exhaustion takes him. Agency and vulnerability meet without sentimentality. | High |
+| Humor / warmth | 8 | 8 | Chapter 53, lines 27–47: Vastin silently makes room, the broad man's first word to the six is “Aye,” the two injured men resemble badly spaced gateposts, and the boy is physically prevented from blurting. The humor comes from earned relationships, not deflation of danger. | High |
+| Action / suspense | 8 | 9 | Chapter 50, lines 55–157: the three-breath advance, Cael holding Teague's left, the bodily line of Force, recoil, and the realization that “It was width.” Geography, adaptation, and cost are trackable. The embedded markers are the only major damage; the developed fight should remain. | High |
+| Progression payoff | 8 | 9 | Chapter 50, line 129, the thirteenth acquisition; chapter 53, lines 89–121, Cael carefully aligns it, hears the cost in his old ribs, and declines to fire it. Prior observation becomes capability, but restraint—not spectacle—is the payoff. | High |
+| Connection | 8 | 9 | Chapter 52, lines 145–205, joins the old year, prior rings, repeated crossings, the lamp finding, and Karis's refusal to bridge two pages without evidence. Dates, injuries, route records, and relationship promises carry forward coherently. | High |
+| Read-aloud quality | 4 | 6 | Chapter 50's count and breath pattern and chapter 53's fire scene have excellent oral cadence. The ten bracketed notes are unperformable, and the object/referent load in chapter 52, lines 117–221, is harder to follow without the page in view. | High |
+
+## Editorial findings
+
+### 1. Release blocker: protected-text placeholders remain in the prose
+
+Ten raw Tier-B notes occur at chapter 49 lines 99 and 169; chapter 50 lines 113, 173, 177, and 245; chapter 51 lines 21 and 323; chapter 52 line 265; and chapter 53 line 291. They replace, respectively, “They knew”; the “Nobody declares…” exchange; “Through”; “Nothing was gained inside”; “By count”; “You'll die in there” / “We've been in three times”; the three-line arm warning; the bearing “Through”; “The Compact … Yes. Part of it”; and the S20 closing exchange.
+
+This is not cosmetic markup. The notes expose planning logic, offer alternative speakers, and tell a coordinator what to write. They interrupt the central fight, the injury aftermath, the Compact disclosure, and the movement's closing hook. Because several units are protected wording, ordinary paraphrase is not an acceptable repair. Speaker assignment and minimal staging must respect the sequence locks already cited in the notes: the tall man and older healer remain silent to the six; Oryn owns “Everybody says that now”; and the S20 alternation begins with Karis.
+
+### 2. The evidence sequence is intellectually strong but audio-dense
+
+Chapter 52, especially lines 117–221, asks the reader to track several physical documents and several meanings of “page” at once. The logical chain is sound: the old year is narrowed, the lamp behavior is separated from its cause, Karis moves her measured leaf away from the folded testimony, and Cael keeps a third page off the blanket. On paper, the spatial metaphor rewards attention. For a thirteen-year-old listening, “the hide,” “the clean sheet,” “six sheets,” “the notebook,” “the ruled leaf,” “a folded paper,” “two pages,” and “a third page” can momentarily blur object, document, and category.
+
+The answer is not to simplify the discovery or collapse the two pages; their separation is the moral and epistemic center of the chapter. A very small orientation pass—reasserting which physical object sits at which end of the blanket at one or two transitions, and ensuring pronouns have unmistakable antecedents—would preserve the reasoning while lowering working-memory load.
+
+### 3. Story and character architecture are working
+
+The movement has a clear escalation: road competence, a site reading, reconnaissance, a fight solved by width, an evidentiary discovery, and a controlled approach to the next danger. Teague's field knowledge becomes Cael's bodily lesson; Karis's discipline stops inference from becoming fact; Vastin's history becomes useful without making him the solver; and the young one earns attachment through deeds. The best choice is Cael's refusal to test Force in chapter 53. It makes progression costly and ethical, preserves Teague's knowledge boundary, and converts a new ability into character rather than fireworks.
+
+## Canon and continuity audit
+
+No verified canon contradiction was found against the supplied `BOOK_MAP`, `STATE_LEDGER` through movement 7, `CANON_RULES`, `UNIVERSE_BIBLE`, and movement plan. The following checks passed:
+
+- **Calendar and resources:** days 299–305 progress in order; Vastin moves from day 20 to day 26; Oryn's cairn passage begins on day 300 and advances consistently; the purse drops from 127 to 123 and then holds.
+- **Progression state:** the seep raises confirmed deployment from 32 to 33. The Span yields the thirteenth acquired fragment, Force-adjacent, but chapter 53's dry alignment does not fire it and therefore does not add a deployment.
+- **Power and knowledge limits:** Teague is not told that Cael acquired his capability. Cael refuses activation near camp and before consulting the healer. The tall man does not speak to the six; the older healer remains silent; the broad man's “Aye” at chapter 53 line 33 is his first word to the six.
+- **Bodies and consent:** Teague's arm and the broad man's leg carry real cost beyond the fight. Oryn asks permission before touching the shin at chapter 53 lines 41–47. Violence remains consequential and non-gory.
+- **Reserved disclosures:** Karis states only what the measurements support. The two pages remain separate, the seals remain unnamed, and the prose does not introduce the forbidden terminal/circuit/infrastructure explanation or disclose the reserved cause early.
+- **Documents and objects:** the copied signs, fixed log, tapes, directive, objection, and separate leaves remain distinct. Seln's case stays shut and its contents stay unnamed.
+
+The universe material's legacy description of Rune as “partial Bronze” is superseded here by the protected notice's “Tier equivalent unknown,” as directed by `BOOK_MAP` conflict ruling C5; the manuscript follows that ruling.
+
+## Protected-wording audit
+
+I checked every protected unit in `BOOK_MAP` that falls inside this movement.
+
+Rendered wording is intact in the thirteenth-fragment notice (chapter 50 line 129), the fixed win sentence (50:301), the S19 log (51:339), the lamp finding (52:181), the ruler line (52:197), the directive (52:239), the objection (52:249), the crack line (52:261), the broad man's first “Aye” (53:33), and the final sentence (53:293). No substitution drift was found in those rendered units.
+
+The ten other applicable Tier-B units have not been rendered at all; their placeholders are listed in Finding 1. The protected final sentence, “He was right. He did not yet know how right,” is present, but the protected S20 exchange immediately before it is still a note, so the closer is not yet complete.
+
+## Reader Standard
+
+The movement passes the content standard for a thirteen-year-old: language is clean; there is no sexual content or innuendo; the fighting avoids gore; harm has aftermath; and consent is explicit before healing. Its moral center is unusually clear without preaching: nobody is left under the barricade, the defeated watch is not pursued, water is shared, an enemy's head is kept off stone, Karis refuses to turn inference into fact, and Cael refuses an unsafe secret test.
+
+Vocabulary is highly accessible, but accessibility scores do not remove the chapter 52 listening burden or the role-name load (“broad man,” “tall man,” “young one,” two healers) during fast action. Those design choices remain intelligible because behavior differentiates the cast; the limited orientation repair proposed above is sufficient. The raw coordinator notes are the only absolute Reader Standard failure because they are not story prose.
+
+## Source reuse
+
+Using the supplied `source_overlap.py` result, there are **0 unprotected shared runs of eight or more words** and **18 protected runs**, which are allowed. There is no source-reuse finding.
+
+## Numerical formula alignment
+
+### Coverage and method
+
+The supplied measurement covers all seven chapters: 38,009 prose words, 2,701 sentences, 1,086 written paragraphs, and 32 marked scene breaks. I used the provided output and did not re-estimate it. The method is `editions/monroe-1.3/tools/formula_metrics.py` as described in its module docstring: Markdown headings and marked breaks are stripped for sentence/readability analysis; paragraph units are nonempty Markdown lines; scene breaks are exact marked separators; sentences are split by a punctuation/whitespace/capitalization heuristic with abbreviation protection; and syllables use a vowel-group heuristic with silent-e/-le handling. Proper names and system terms are processed by that same heuristic.
+
+One qualification matters: `words_in_system_notices` is reported as 0 even though ten bracketed editorial placeholders remain in the chapter files. Those notes are therefore included in the reported prose population rather than excluded as notices. The supplied values are the required baseline, but formula compliance is provisional until the protected text is restored and the same tool is rerun.
+
+### Measured results
+
+| Metric | Target | Observed | Editorial assessment |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| Mean sentence length | 14.6 words; working range 13–15.5 | 14.07 | Pass |
+| Median sentence length | 11 | 11 | Exact |
+| Sentence SD, population | about 26 | 11.02 | Material departure: much narrower distribution |
+| Sentences ≤5 words | 27.7%; working ceiling about 34% | 23.6% | Below the modeled texture target, though not outside the edition's stated ceiling |
+| Sentences ≥40 words | 3.3%; working range 2.5–4.5% | 3.8% | Pass |
+| Written paragraph mean | 26.8-word ASR proxy | 35.0 | Longer than the directional proxy |
+| Written paragraph median | 18-word ASR proxy; working ceiling about 30 | 24.0 | Pass working range; comparison remains directional |
+| Scene breaks per 10k | about 8.7 | 8.42 | Close alignment |
+| Words per scene | about 950; working range 850–1,050 | 974.6 | Pass |
+| Flesch Reading Ease | 72.3 | 94.5 | Large numerical departure toward easier prose |
+| Flesch–Kincaid grade | 6.8; working range 3.5–6 | 3.57 | Passes the edition's working range narrowly, but is far below the exact model target |
+
+The three primary working checks—sentence mean, long-sentence share, and words per scene—pass. Scene rhythm is particularly well aligned. Median sentence length is exact, while short-sentence share is 4.1 percentage points below the model target and population spread is far narrower than the requested wide-spike texture. In practice, the prose often alternates short paragraphs with moderate sentences rather than setting many very short blows beside genuinely long compound-complex runs.
+
+Flesch and grade results should be reported, not overinterpreted. The one-syllable concrete lexicon (“stick,” “line,” “road,” “stone,” “hand”) drives the estimate toward extreme ease, while the evidence logic and unnamed-role tracking create conceptual difficulty that the formula cannot see. A global vocabulary inflation to chase 6.8 would harm the Reader Standard. Any cadence repair should instead be local and syntactic after the placeholders are replaced.
+
+### Unmeasured formula components
+
+- **Progression-callout density and third placement:** UNMEASURED. No project-specific lexicon/count was supplied, and this movement alone cannot verify the full-book 1.7× front-loading ratio. Qualitatively, this closing-third movement uses system language at genuine turns—the seep reading, the thirteenth acquisition, and the dry alignment—rather than reteaching continuously, which matches the intended late-book shape.
+- **Development cadence:** UNMEASURED as a rate. Manual evidence is distributed rather than concentrated: Cael accepts bodily instruction and declines the unsafe test; the young one acts without being ordered; Teague trusts his left side; Karis enforces evidentiary discipline; Vastin accepts being stopped; Seln changes how he reads the pass; and Oryn and the older healer cooperate without violating consent or silence locks.
+- **POV word share:** UNMEASURED. Segment inspection shows Cael remains dominant, with brief secondary-focus cutaways to Seln in chapter 49, Teague in chapter 51, and Karis in chapter 53. That is structurally consistent with an approximately 87/13 single-lead design, but no precise share should be claimed.
+- **Secondary signals:** UNMEASURED. No published movement-specific lexicons/counts were supplied for adverbs, tags, combat terms, fillers, or repeated phrases; they should not be inferred by impression.
+
+### Formula judgment
+
+The movement aligns on its primary accepted ranges and on scene cadence, while missing the reference texture's extreme sentence-length spread and exact readability center. Those departures do not justify broad rewriting before the placeholders are fixed: the notes contaminate the measurements, and the strongest action and character scenes already have purposeful rhythm. After restoration, rerun the same tool once; if the narrow spread persists, make a bounded cadence pass in exposition rather than shortening the Span fight or complicating diction.
+
