+
+The three primary working checks—sentence mean, long-sentence share, and words per scene—pass. Scene rhythm is particularly well aligned. Median sentence length is exact, while short-sentence share is 4.1 percentage points below the model target and population spread is far narrower than the requested wide-spike texture. In practice, the prose often alternates short paragraphs with moderate sentences rather than setting many very short blows beside genuinely long compound-complex runs.
+
+Flesch and grade results should be reported, not overinterpreted. The one-syllable concrete lexicon (“stick,” “line,” “road,” “stone,” “hand”) drives the estimate toward extreme ease, while the evidence logic and unnamed-role tracking create conceptual difficulty that the formula cannot see. A global vocabulary inflation to chase 6.8 would harm the Reader Standard. Any cadence repair should instead be local and syntactic after the placeholders are replaced.
